1. Definitions

"Licensor" is BWJ Tech Ltd. "You" is the individual or the legal entity
exercising the rights granted here. A "Licence Key" is a signed token issued
by the Licensor that names You, the features You may run and the date the key
expires. "Internal Use" is use by You and by Your employees and contractors,
for Your own purposes, and not on behalf of a third party.

2. What You may do without a Licence Key

You may read, copy, compile and modify the Enterprise Software for the
purposes of inspecting it, auditing it, testing it and contributing to it. The
source is here to be read. Nothing in this section permits running the
Enterprise Software in production.

3. What a Licence Key permits

While You hold a valid Licence Key that has not expired, You may run the
Enterprise Software in production for Internal Use, for the features the key
names, and You may modify it for Internal Use. There is no limit on the number
of websites You measure or the number of people who use the dashboard, unless
the key itself names one.

4. What You may not do

You may not distribute, sublicense, sell, rent, lease or otherwise make the
Enterprise Software available to any third party, in source or in compiled
form. You may not operate the Enterprise Software as a service for any third
party. You may not remove, disable, circumvent or reimplement the licence
check, and You may not remove or alter any copyright or licence notice. You
may not use the Enterprise Software to build a product that competes with
Chokh.

5. Contributions

A contribution You make to the Enterprise Software is governed by the
contributor licence agreement in CLA.md at the root of the repository. It does
not grant You any right to run the Enterprise Software beyond this licence.

6. Term and termination

This licence runs for as long as Your Licence Key is valid. It terminates
immediately if You breach any term of section 4, and on the expiry of Your
Licence Key. On termination You must stop running the Enterprise Software in
production. Section 2 survives termination, and so does Your licence to every
other part of the Chokh repository, which is MIT and is not affected by
anything here.

